      "duration": "04:24",
      "video_id": "ZfulxtgNv9U",
      "lead_quote": "That's the chance you got if you got a friend / Yeah, seventy-six percent",
      "lyrics": "[Verse 1]\nI was at a meetin' in a church basement\nThe coffee's bad, but the chairs are warm\nI'm just tryin' to get my bearings\nIn the quiet after the storm\nA fella gets up, he's readin' from a paper\nTalkin' 'bout studies, and what they found\nAnd he said a number...\nThat knocked me right back on the ground\n[Chorus]\nHe said... Seventy-six...\nThat's the chance you got if you got a friend\nYeah, seventy-six percent\nThat your broken life will mend\nBut all alone...\nThe number's thirty-two\nAnd I just... sat there\nAnd all I thought about... was you\n[Verse 2]\n'Cause I know those numbers, I've lived 'em\nI was thirty-two, and fallin' fast\nA ghost on a frozen window pane\nA story that was never meant to last\nI was a statistic in the alley\nJust a \"problem to resolve\"\nA two-milligram gamble\nThat the cold gray snow would solve\n[Chorus]\nBut you... you were seventy-six\nYou were the hand that pulled me through\nFrom that lonely, freezin' thirty-two\nThat I was chained myself onto\nYou're the forty-four percent\nYou're the difference, Joe, it's true\nYou're not just my unlikely friend\nYou're the odds... I beat... 'cause of you\n[Bridge]\nThe opposite of addiction...\nIs not sobriety, I see\nIt's not a pill, or a program\nIt's the connection... between you and me\nIt's the hamburger at the mall\nIt's the fight to get the card\nIt's the simple, steady presence\nThat makes a man drop his guard\n[Chorus]\nYeah, I'm at seventy-six\n'Cause you refused to let me be\nJust another lonely number\nThat nobody else could see\nYou're the forty-four percent\nMy forty-four-point friend\nWho sat with me in the food court\nAnd brought the story to an end...\n...or made it start\nSeventy-six\n[Outro]\nSeventy-six...\nThirty-two...\nThank you, Joe",
      "story": "This is the intellectual and emotional thesis of the entire album, a stark acoustic ballad that lays bare the \"why\" of William's recovery. William, in a quiet, confessional vocal, reflects on a statistic he has learned—that the probability of recovery with high social support is 76%, versus only 32% for those with low support. He processes, in real-time, that his friend Joe is not just a kind man but the literal, statistical \"44-point difference\" between survival and relapse. The song transforms the album's narrative from a simple story of kindness into a profound statement on social connection as a life-saving, structural intervention.\n\nNarratively, this movement represents (Acoustic Ballad w/ Cello) The core statistic. A stark reflection on the numbers: \"With a friend, you got a 76 percent chance. All alone, it's 32.\". William reflects that Joe is that 44-point difference.. The Thematic Core. This is the intellectual and emotional heart of Act IV, directly explaining the why behind the success of Track 10. It states the album's thesis: connection is a statistical, life-saving intervention.",
