      "video_id": "flLsbRPukXk",
      "lead_quote": "Oh, the opposite of addiction / Is not sobriety / It's connection...",
      "lyrics": "[Verse 1]\nWe want to draw a simple, solid line\nBetween the righteous and the weak\nWe want a cure that's chemical\nA fix that's fast and quick\nWe blame the frailty, we blame the sin\nWe build a wall and lock 'em in\nWe never ask about the cold\nOr the broken world they're standin' in\n[Chorus]\nOh, the opposite of addiction\nIs not sobriety\nIt's connection...\n...it's the thing we've lost\nThe thing we're told to never see\nIt's the hamburger at the food court\nIt's the fight to get the card\nIt's the seein' of the human\nIn a life that's been so hard\n[Verse 2]\nWe're all addicted, in our own way\nTo the comfort and the light\nTo the other side of the window\nThat keeps the alley from our sight\nAddicted to the 'us and them'\nThe judgment that just keeps us warm\nThe wall we build between our hearts\nTo keep us safe from their storm\n[Chorus]\nBut the opposite of addiction\nIs not sobriety\nIt's connection...\n...it's the thing we've lost\nThe thing we're told to never see\nIt's the hamburger at the food court\nIt's the fight to get the card\nIt's the seein' of the human\nIn a life that's been so hard\n[Bridge]\nThis 'Divide and Conquer' story\nIs the deadliest seed we sow\nIt's the 'us and them' that kills the man\nThat we will never know\nIt's the 'us and them' that makes the cold\nThat lets the Fentanyl win\nAnd the only cure... the only one\nIs to let the 'other' in\n[Chorus]\n'Cause the opposite of addiction\nIs not sobriety\nIt's connection...\n...it's the thing we've lost\nThe thing we're told to never see\nIt's the hamburger at the food court\nIt's the fight to get the card\nIt's the seein' of the human\nIn a life that's been so hard\n[Outro]\nIt's connection\nJust connection\nThe opposite...",
      "story": "This slow, deliberate acoustic folk song is the album's formal thesis statement, the \"moral of the story.\" Shifting from William's personal narrative to the Bard's universal one, the song \"zooms out\" to argue that the true antidote to the \"shady\" world we've seen is not a program or a pill, but human connection. It directly states that \"the opposite of addiction is not sobriety, it's connection\"—a connection that the modern world of division (the \"us and them\") is designed to break. It transforms William's story from a singular tale of kindness into a powerful, actionable lesson for the listener.\n\nNarratively, this movement represents (Acoustic Folk w/ Cello) A slow, deliberate song. \"The opposite of addiction is not sobriety / It's connection\". This song turns the album's story into a universal message.. The \"Moral of the Story.\" This track zooms out from William's specific story (Track 13) to speak directly to the listener and connect to the Bard's core mission of healing division.",
